    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49880" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰδῐό-στολος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>equipped at one's own
				expense</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τριήρης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Alc.</u>
					1
				</span></i>
			; <i>hired for one's own use</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλοῖον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ath.
					12.521a
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
				<u>VA</u>
				5.20
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰ. πλεῦσαι</span> sail <i>in
				one's own ship</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Thes.</u>
				26
			</span></i>.</div>
